/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let x[n] be a length-N sequence, n = 0, 1, ..., N−1.
   - X[k] = Σn=0N−1 x[n] WNnk
   - X[k] is the kth DFT value, k = 0, ..., N−1; x[n] is the input sequence; WN = e−j2π/N is the twiddle factor.
   - The inverse DFT returns x[n] from X[k].
   - x[n] = (1/N) Σk=0N−1 X[k] WN−nk
   - x[n] is the recovered sequence; X[k] is the DFT; 1/N is the synthesis scale factor.
   - For a length-N sequence, X[k] equals the DTFT X(ejω) at ω = 2πk/N.
   - In matrix form X = W x.
   - The DFT treats x[n] as one period of a periodic sequence of period N.
   - y[n] = x[(n−m) mod N] → Y[k] = WNkm X[k]
*/
