/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - X(z) = Σn=−∞∞ x[n] z−n
   - x[n] is the sequence; z is a complex number; n is an integer index.
   - Write z = r ejθ, where r = |z| is the radius and θ is the angle.
   - If z = ejω, then r = 1 and X(ejω) = Σ x[n] e−jωn, the DTFT of chapter 6.2.
   - Convergence depends on r, not on θ.
   - Four cases cover most exam questions.
   - The unit circle is the set |z| = 1.
   - For a = 1/3, both sequences give z/(z − 1/3), but the right-sided one has ROC |z| > 1/3 and the left-sided one has ROC |z| < 1/3.
*/
